@startuml

title The retry verb

class "retry verb" as retry <<message>> #E1F5FF {
    +tenant : tenant id
    +run : instance id
    +from step : text
}

class "retry answer" as answer <<message>> #E8F5E9 {
    +run : instance id
    +step index : number
    +step : text
    +refusal : text
}

retry --> answer : answers

note top of retry
Resumes a stopped run: the caller asks for the failed step again.
- tenant: the tenant the run belongs to.
- run: the run to resume.
- from step: the step to resume from; absent when the
  run resumes from the step that failed.
end note

note bottom of answer
The answer names the step the engine re-dispatched, or why it
refused: a run that has not stopped, a step the run does not
hold, or a step whose predecessors have not all completed.
end note

@enduml
